# Channel table for HEPMC_GENERATOR=gibuu_mix (prod_gibuu/generator_gibuu_mix.sh):
# MicroBooNE BNB numu, numubar, nue, nuebar x CC, NC on argon.
#
# Columns:
#   name  process_ID  flavor_ID  nuExp  nu_pdg  ccnc  equalWeights_Max  numEnsembles  sigma  flux  enrich
# sigma  flux-averaged cross section, 1e-38 cm2 per nucleon, for gibuu_BNB_numuCC.job physics
#        (GiBUU 2025 patch 5) and the MCC9 flux tables (data/flux/BNB_*_uboone_mcc9.dat)
# flux   integral of that flux table [nu/POT/cm2] (make_flux_table.py normalisation)
# enrich sampling enhancement e_c (1 = natural mixture, all event weights 1); a channel with
#        e_c != 1 is drawn e_c times more often and its events get weight p_c/q_c
#
# Max / numEnsembles only change the speed (the mixture is set by the drawn counts):
#   Max >= ~3x the largest trial weight seen (CC tails reach ~1600 in 5e6 trials, NC 539);
#   few ensembles for the rare channels so that their GiBUU runs are short.
#
# sigma sources (2026-10-19):
#   numuCC    0.8056 +- 0.0053  100-job grid production (200 time steps)
#   numuNC    0.2884 +- 0.0024  weighted calibrations 0.2882+-0.0025 (8 jobs) and 0.2898+-0.0072 (calmix)
#   others    weighted calibration, 6 runs x 500 ensembles each, numTimeSteps=0
#             (numTimeSteps does not change the inclusive cross section; checked on numu CC/NC)
#   errors:   numubarCC 2.9%  numubarNC 5.7%  nueCC 1.8%  nueNC 2.5%  nuebarCC 2.5%  nuebarNC 2.5%
#
# name     proc flav nuExp  pdg ccnc   Max  nEns   sigma   flux        enrich
numuCC       2   2   21     14   0   5000  2000   0.8056  7.3762e-10  1
numuNC       3   2   21     14   1   2000  2000   0.2884  7.3762e-10  1
numubarCC   -2   2   22    -14   0   2000   500   0.1013  4.5589e-11  1
numubarNC   -3   2   22    -14   1   2000   200   0.0566  4.5589e-11  1
nueCC        2   1   19     12   0   5000   200   0.9433  3.9779e-12  1
nueNC        3   1   19     12   1   2000   200   0.2987  3.9779e-12  1
nuebarCC    -2   1   20    -12   0   5000   200   0.3010  4.0255e-13  1
nuebarNC    -3   1   20    -12   1   2000   200   0.1268  4.0255e-13  1
